---
// The App Store and Google Play listings link to /privacy, so keep this URL.
// Update the date whenever the policy changes.
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../site.mjs";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How the Unum app handles your information."
>
  <article class="container section policy split">
    <h1 class="full">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated full">Last updated: October 20, 2026</p>

    <p class="full intro-line">Unum is a civic literacy app. We are committed to protecting your privacy.</p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>
      We collect push notification tokens solely to deliver bill and official
      update notifications you opt into. These tokens are stored on our secure
      server and are never sold or shared with third parties.
    </p>
    <p>
      During onboarding, you may optionally provide a zip code to identify your
      congressional district. This zip code is stored on your device and on our
      secure server solely to deliver relevant notifications.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you type a street address on the congressional map, the text you type
      is sent from your device to Mapbox to suggest matching addresses, and the
      address you search is sent to the U.S. Census Bureau Geocoder to find its
      congressional district. Mapbox also uses your device's IP address to show
      nearby addresses first. We do not store the addresses you type or search,
      on your device or on our server.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we do not collect</h2>
    <p>
      We do not collect your name, email address, or any personally
      identifiable information. We do not use third-party analytics or
      advertising SDKs. We do not sell your data.
    </p>

    <h2>Data storage</h2>
    <p>
      Your lists, followed bills, and app preferences are stored locally on
      your device. Your zip code and notification preferences are stored on our
      secure server solely to deliver relevant notifications.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Unum relies on the following services. When the app loads content from
      them, they receive standard technical information such as your device's
      IP address, as with any website or app that loads content online.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Push notifications:</strong> Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM)
        delivers push notifications, governed by Google's Privacy Policy at
        <a class="text-link" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legislative data:</strong> provided by the Congress.gov API from
        the Library of Congress. Member photos are loaded from the Biographical
        Directory of the United States Congress.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Zip code lookup:</strong> zip codes are matched to congressional
        districts using U.S. Census Bureau data stored on our server.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Congressional map:</strong> district boundaries and street
        address lookup are provided by the U.S. Census Bureau. Address
        suggestions are provided by Mapbox, governed by its privacy policy at
        <a class="text-link" href="https://www.mapbox.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mapbox.com/legal/privacy</a>.
        Map images are
        loaded from the OpenStreetMap Foundation's servers, governed by its
        privacy policy at
        <a class="text-link" href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy</a>.
        The map is displayed with the open-source Leaflet library, loaded from
        the unpkg content delivery network. Map data ©
        <a class="text-link" href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>,
        available under the Open Database License.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Unum is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect
      information from children under 13.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Continued use of the
      app constitutes acceptance of any changes.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions, contact us at
      <a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
      or through the Report an Error feature in the app.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy {
    padding-top: var(--intro-top);
  }

  .policy h1 {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .updated {
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-size: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .policy h2 {
    font-size: 26px;
    margin: 44px 0 12px;
  }

  .policy p + p {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  /* Two-column layout: each heading and its first paragraph share a row, so
     they get the same top spacing */
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .policy > h2,
    .policy > h2 + * {
      margin-top: 44px;
    }

    .policy > h2 {
      margin-bottom: 0;
      font-size: 22px;
      line-height: 1.3;
    }
  }

  .policy p,
  .policy li {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .policy ul {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }
</style>
